WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.110
In fiscal year 2009, the
federal deficit reached about

2
00:00:04.110 --> 00:00:06.470
10 percent of GDP.

3
00:00:06.470 --> 00:00:11.420
That year, Congress passed a stimulus
worth about 800 billion dollars.

4
00:00:11.420 --> 00:00:15.070
But that vote explains only
part of the jump in borrowing.

5
00:00:15.070 --> 00:00:18.110
So why does a government's
borrowing jump in a recession,

6
00:00:18.110 --> 00:00:20.390
even when nobody votes for it?

7
00:00:20.390 --> 00:00:22.950
In this mission, you'll
use a graph lab and watch

8
00:00:22.950 --> 00:00:25.720
a fall in spending ripple
through the economy,

9
00:00:25.720 --> 00:00:27.360
round by round.

10
00:00:27.360 --> 00:00:30.220
Then you'll compare fast and slow policy,

11
00:00:30.220 --> 00:00:32.650
and see why time lags matter.

12
00:00:32.650 --> 00:00:37.640
Your mission: figure out what drives
borrowing up when nobody decides to.
